AOWIS Server Map — Debian installation
======================================

Service:       aowis-server-map.service
Binary:        /usr/bin/aowis-server-map
Vendor unit:   /usr/lib/systemd/system/aowis-server-map.service
Configuration: /etc/aowis-server-map/map-server.ini
Provider state: /var/lib/aowis-server-map/providers.ini
Cache root:    /var/cache/aowis-server-map/

On first installation, the package creates a service account and an
administrator INI containing independent, randomly generated read and delete
API keys. If the INI exists, the package preserves its content and permissions.
It does not merge or replace administrator configuration during upgrades.

The service runs as the unprivileged aowis-server-map user and provisions
/var/lib and /var/cache using systemd StateDirectory= and CacheDirectory=.
ProtectSystem=strict prevents the running service from writing to /etc.

The GUI/map provider API can replace the raster provider catalog at runtime.
It writes only /var/lib/aowis-server-map/providers.ini; /etc still controls
all other server configuration. The provider state is created on the first
successful save and persists across restarts and upgrades. To return to the
provider list in /etc, stop the service and back up/remove providers.ini.

Validate the installed configuration without starting a listener:

  sudo aowis-server-map --check-config --config /etc/aowis-server-map/map-server.ini

See the complete built-in defaults without changing configuration:

  aowis-server-map --print-default-config

Use administrator-managed systemd drop-ins rather than editing the vendor unit:

  sudo systemctl edit aowis-server-map
  sudo systemctl cat aowis-server-map

Administration:

  sudo systemctl status aowis-server-map
  sudo journalctl -u aowis-server-map -f
  sudo systemctl restart aowis-server-map

The package installs two Apache reverse-proxy templates disabled:

  /etc/apache2/sites-available/aowis-map.localhost.conf
  /etc/apache2/sites-available/aowis-server-map.conf

Enable only the template appropriate for the installation, after replacing its
sample domain/backend/origin values. Internet-facing deployments must terminate
HTTPS at the proxy and restrict direct network access to the map-server port.
The map-provider PUT API currently has no authentication; only trusted clients
may reach it.

More instructions: /usr/share/doc/aowis-server-map/ or the source repository's
README.md and configs/systemd/README.md.
